  "script": "This is the lightest and most powerful M5 ever made, weighing in 230 pounds less than its siblings. That's the BMW M5 CS. BMW produced only 1,132 units of the M5 CS during its 2022 model year run, with 454 of them allocated to the United States. Under the hood, a 4.4-liter turbocharged V8 churns out 627 horsepower and 553 lb-ft of torque, sent to all four wheels. It's crafted for performance with extensive use of carbon fiber, shedding unnecessary weight to boost agility. Originally priced at $142,000, they go for about $172,233 today\u2014proof of how coveted this limited-run beast has become. So, would you take this upgraded, four-seat powerhouse for a daily drive, or is it strictly for the weekends?",
